'''Tabanan''', officially the '''Imperial State of Tabanan''' ([[Tabanese language|Tabanese]]: ''Karahanan Sabyang it Tabanan''), is a sovereign island nation occupying the northern portion of the continent of [[Almuria (continent)|Almuria]]. It is divided into five federal provinces, two territories, and a capital district. Tabanan has an area of 795,306 square kilometers (307,070 sq mi) with a population of 19 million people. The nation's capital is [[Balete City|Balete]] while the largest city is [[Paralaya]].

Tabanan's territory consists of a large mainland, which accounts for roughly five-sixths of the national area, together with fifteen smaller offshore islands. The country lies wholly within the northern tropics. Its only land border is shared with [[Pakiak]], the southern Almurian state; everywhere else the frontier is maritime, with a coastline of approximately 4,890 kilometers.

==Etymology==
The origin of the name ''Tabanan'' is TBA. In the official [[Tabanese language|Tabanese]] name of the state, ''Karahanan Sabyang it Tabanan'', the element ''karahanan'' denotes a kingdom or royal realm, so the full title may be rendered as "the Royal Realm of Tabanan."

