==Geography==
Tabanan occupies the northern portion of the Almurian mainland and its adjacent islands, between longitudes 132.5°E and 142.2°E and latitudes 10.2°N and 21.7°N. The mainland covers approximately 669,500 km², about 84 percent of the national territory; the remainder is distributed among fifteen offshore islands, the largest of which measures roughly 1,000 km². The total coastline measures approximately 4,890 km. Tabanan's southern frontier with [[Pakiak]] follows the <> mountain range.

===Climate===
Lying wholly within the northern tropics, Tabanan has a tropical climate; regional variation across the provinces is TBA.

